PVD("myanmar_vision_2018-2030",{"docs":["","Myanmar MSDP 2018 2030 1"],"s":{"1":[[1,"2","22","Investment Enabling Environment Reform","Provide a secure, conducive investment enabling environment which eases the cost of doing business, boosts investor confidence and increases efficiencies",""],[1,"2","22","Trade Sector Reform and Cooperation Strengthening","Further reform our trade sector and strengthen regional and international cooperation",""],[1,"8","2","Trade Policy Revision","Trade policies have been, and continue to be, revised in line with regional and global commitments and in accordance with liberal principles.",""],[1,"8","2","Investment Policy Revision","Investment policies likewise have been revised with the aim of ensuring a level playing field for all investors, and to create in Myanmar a favourable, predictable and friendly investment climate.",""],[1,"8","6","Inclusive Private Sector Development Promotion","The GoM continues to encourage equitable and inclusive private sector development (the true and most reliable engine of growth)",""],[1,"13","13","Private Sector Growth and Investment Promotion Measures","Asserting the right of individuals to freely pursue the economic opportunities they choose, so as to enable private sector growth in line with a market economy system; formulating specific policies to increase foreign investment; and strengthening property rights and the rule of law.",""],[1,"32","4","Investment Climate and Finance Access Strengthening","Accordingly, the strategies under Goal 3 are formulated with the recognition that the government has a critical role to play in improving the enabling environment in order to stimulate foreign and domestic investment, increasing access to finance, strengthening existing partnerships, and forging new linkages with the global and regional communities.",""],[1,"36","3","Inclusive Trade and Investment Environment Reform","Create a robust environment for sustainable trade and investment to grow inclusively (PSD-AP Pillar 3)",""],[1,"37","2","Secure and Conducive Investment Enabling Environment","Provide a secure, conducive investment enabling environment",""],[1,"37","3","Systematic and Transparent Regulatory Enforcement","Ensure the systematic, predicable, and transparent enforcement of rules, procedures, notifications, orders, directives and permits",""],[1,"39","11","Enabling Environment for Sustainable Trade and Investment","Robust environment for sustainable trade and investment to grow inclusively (PSD-AP Pillar 3)",""],[1,"39","12","Enabling Policy and Legislative Reform for Investment and Efficiency","Introduce a robust, innovative enabling policy and legislative environment which promotes efficient practices and facilitates greater investment without sacrificing potential revenue generation",""]],"2":[[1,"2","21","Support Job Creation in Industry and Services","Strategy 3.2: Support job creation in industry and services, especially through developing small-and medium-",""],[1,"18","1","MSME Incubation and Productivity Support Initiative","incubating and unlocking the entrepreneurial and productivity potential of our micro-, small- and medium-sized enterprises will become an important driver of income and employment generation in post-conflict and conflict-affected communities.",""],[1,"32","6","Inclusive and Equitable Job Creation and Labour Market Governance","Attention is paid throughout to ensuring that job creation and labour market governance is inclusive and equitable, with a particular focus on increasing access to decent, safe and quality work for women and other vulnerable groups.",""],[1,"35","6","Support for Job Creation in Medium-Sized Enterprises","Support job creation in industry medium-sized enterprises",""],[1,"36","3","SME Development for Local and Regional Growth","Enhanced role of SMEs in local, sub-national and regional development (MTP-AFT Pillar 4);",""],[1,"36","6","Incentives for SME, SMI and Foreign Investment in Myanmar Enterprises","Create appropriate incentives for SME, SMI and foreign firms to invest in Myanmar enterprises (both financially and in skills transfer) without sacrificing revenue generation potential",""],[1,"37","11","Administrative Simplification for SMEs and SMIs","Improve administrative practices and procedures to reduce compliance burden and transaction costs for SMEs and SMIs",""]],"3":[[1,"8","6","State Economic Enterprise Reform and Corporatisation","The GoM is encouraging its State Economic Enterprises (SEEs) to transform into non-budgeted units, and then into corporatised units that will eventually be equitised to the private sector",""],[1,"8","6","Capacity Building for Enterprise Reform Delivery","the GoM recognises that significant capacity building is required in delivering such outcomes",""],[1,"13","8","State-Owned Enterprise Reform and Privatization","Improving the operations of State-owned enterprises and privatising those State-owned enterprises that have the potential to be reformed, while promoting and assisting small and medium enterprises as generators of employment and growth.",""],[1,"24","1","State Economic Enterprise Efficiency and Competitiveness Improvement","enhancing the efficiency and competitiveness of SEEs",""],[1,"30","7","State Economic Enterprise Governance Reform","As such, improved SEE governance shall be key to both mobilising fiscal resources for the GoM and unlocking the country's economic potential.",""],[1,"30","8","State Economic Enterprise Reform Agenda","Therefore, the GoM intends to reform SEEs by re-categorising them according to function, reforming their financing formulae, professionalising their management and operations, enhancing oversight and transparency, and, where appropriate, equitizing or privatising assets in a manner that will improve Myanmar's economic performance.",""],[1,"31","1","National Social and Environmental Enterprise Policy Development","Develop a national SEE policy based on a comprehensive review and assessment of existing SEEs",""],[1,"31","3","State-Owned Enterprise Reform and Privatization","Corporatize, commercialise, restructure, or, where appropriate, privatize SEEs which operate in competitive markets",""],[1,"31","5","State Economic Enterprise Equitization and Strategic Partner Identification","Identify SEEs that should be fully or partially equitized and identify possible strategic partners",""],[1,"31","7","Standardize SEE Financial Reporting and Public Disclosure","Standardize financial reporting structures across SEEs and release financial data on SEEs to the public",""],[1,"31","9","Competitive Salary Scheme for SEE Employees","Develop competitive salary schemes for SEEs employees to boost SEEs competitiveness",""],[1,"44","5","Corporatisation and Equitisation of Government Commercial Entities","GoM entities that have been conducting commercial operations are appropriately transformed through a process of corporatisation and equitisation to encourage greater private sector involvement.",""]],"4":[[1,"8","4","Digital Financial Settlement and Prudential Banking Reform","has been transformed by the application of online and secured systems allowing real- time settlements and securities transactions, and by the progressive implementation of international prudential bank regulations such as the Basel Accords.",""],[1,"8","5","Prudent Fiscal Discipline and Deficit Reduction","the GoM is committed to continuing prudent fiscal discipline and to maintaining the fiscal deficit to no more than around five per cent of Gross Domestic Product (GDP), while steadfastly reducing recourse to central bank financing to negligible levels.",""],[1,"23","15","Macroeconomic Policy Management","establishing appropriate fiscal, monetary and exchange rate policy, improving Myanmar's balance of payments (BOP) and maintaining inflation at an appropriate level.",""],[1,"24","5","Market-Based Exchange Rate Reference Rate","Recently, the CBM has initiated a number of policy measures including the introduction of a market-based reference rate to effectively manage the exchange rate.","Central Bank of Myanmar (CBM)"],[1,"24","9","Exchange Rate Liberalization","Allow the kyat to float more freely in response to market supply and demand",""],[1,"24","11","Exchange Rate Flexibility Reform","Ensure greater exchange rate flexibility as the CBM moves from a foreign exchange auction to an interbank transaction-",""],[1,"25","4","Exchange Rate Intervention Mechanism","Develop an exchange rate intervention mechanism",""],[1,"25","5","Exchange Rate Stabilization Measures","Abnormal exchange rate movements due to shocks will be stabilized",""],[1,"25","6","Inflation Stabilization through Monetary and Fiscal Policy","Stabilize inflation both from a monetary and fiscal policy perspective",""],[1,"25","8","Foreign Exchange Reserve Concentration in the Central Bank","Promote more effective foreign exchange management through concentration of foreign exchange reserves in the CBM",""],[1,"25","14","Foreign Currency Revenue Centralization Mechanism","Develop a mechanism to allow all government foreign currency revenues to flow into national foreign exchange reserves held by the CBM rather than into other State- owned banks",""],[1,"25","15","Foreign Currency Reserve Accumulation","Foreign currency reserves will be accumulated",""],[1,"26","2","Financial Market Development for Monetary Policy Operations","it is crucial that efforts be made to develop the financial markets necessary to achieve monetary policy objectives.",""],[1,"26","6","Monetary Policy Prudence","Continue monetary policy prudence with a view to stabilizing inflation and ensuring balance between economic growth and stability",""],[1,"26","7","Deposit Auction Operations","Continue conducting deposit auctions",""],[1,"26","9","Flexible Bank Reserve Requirement Enforcement","Continue enforcing reserve requirement instructions on banks with flexibility to account for seasonality",""],[1,"26","10","Credit Growth Control for Inflation Stabilization","Credit growth will be controlled to stabilize inflation",""],[1,"26","11","Treasury Securities Auction Strengthening and Public Bond Awareness","Strengthen treasury securities auctions and expand public understanding of bonds, bills and similar instruments",""],[1,"26","13","Auction Interest Budget Support","Acquire sufficient budget to pay higher interest at the auctions to make auctions more effective",""],[1,"26","15","Interbank Money Market Development and Interest Rate Liberalization","Develop the interbank money market, and ultimately liberalize bank interest rates based on borrower risk profiles",""],[1,"26","17","REPO Market Development and Open Market Operations","Develop the REPO market through which the CBM can absorb excess liquidity from the market through open market operations, including possibly REPO auctions",""],[1,"26","18","Central Bank Liquidity Absorption Mechanism","Central bank will be able to use this channel to absorb excess liquidity of the banks to stabilize inflation",""],[1,"27","1","BOP Shock Absorptive Capacity and Foreign Exchange Reserve Strengthening","Strengthen BOP shock absorptive capacity and build up foreign exchange reserves to support a more favourable BOP position",""]],"5":[[1,"14","2","Fair and Efficient Tax System Reform","Establishing a fair and efficient tax system in order to increase government revenues and protecting individual rights and property rights through enacting laws and regulations.",""],[1,"19","1","Intergovernmental Fiscal Transfer Reform","Improve efficiency and equitable distribution of inter-governmental fiscal transfers to States and Regions, and strengthen fiscal capacities of sub- national public entities",""],[1,"27","3","Tax Administration Reform and Modernization","Increasing tax revenue requires a reformed and professional tax administration with high levels of integrity and clear powers to assess and collect tax as well as to manage tax exemptions.",""],[1,"27","3","Taxpayer Compliance Legal Framework","The job also requires a legal framework that encourages taxpayers to meet their tax obligations, as well as the extensive use of modern technology to make it easy for taxpayers to file tax returns and pay tax online.",""],[1,"27","4","Tax System Modernization and Transparency Reform","The MSDP prioritises improvements to Myanmar's tax collection systems by creating an enabling environment in which tax laws are progressively modernised, in which the tax system is made more transparent and in which corruption is addressed.",""],[1,"27","4","Tax Administration Information Technology Investment","The MSDP also prioritises significant investments in information technology",""],[1,"27","4","Tax Education Expansion Programme","The MSDP also prioritises ... expanding tax education through various channels.",""],[1,"27","7","Domestic Revenue Mobilisation through Taxation Reform","Increase domestic revenue mobilisation through a fair, efficient and transparent taxation system",""],[1,"27","8","Tax Administration Structural and Governance Reform","Reform the structure and governance mechanisms of IRD and other relevant entities, and establish functionally based departments organized to best administer the tax system for different groups of taxpayers",""],[1,"27","10","National Electronic Payment System Expansion","Expand electronic payment systems throughout the country",""],[1,"27","12","Information Technology Systems Modernization for Registration and Case Work","Implement new information technology systems for registration, processing, accounting, and case work",""],[1,"28","1","Tax Law Modernization Reform","Develop modern tax laws, including a new Tax Administration Law, a new Income Tax Law and a new VAT Law",""],[1,"28","3","Anti-Corruption and Tax Evasion Counter-Measures","Introduce anti-corruption and tax evasion counter- measures to protect the integrity and reputation of the tax system, including expanding the focus of internal audit and establishing an Internal Affairs Unit",""],[1,"28","5","Expansion of the Self-Assessment System to Medium Taxpayer Offices","Expand the implementation of a Self- Assessment System to Medium Taxpayer Offices.",""],[1,"28","7","Risk-Based Tax Administration and Compliance Improvement Strategy","Implement a risk-based approach to tax administration using a Compliance Improvement Strategy to guide the administration of taxpayer services and enforcement strategies.",""],[1,"28","9","Tax Process and Procedure Streamlining Reform","Streamline tax processes and procedures to reflect good international practice and maximise opportunities provided by modern technology",""],[1,"28","10","Tax Payment Simplification","Tax payment will be more convenient and effective",""],[1,"28","11","IRD Staff Capacity Development and Performance Management Reform","Develop IRD staff capabilities by providing clear expectations of staff roles and responsibilities, relevant training, modern work practices including effective performance management",""]],"6":[[1,"13","7","Transparent and Effective Public Financial Management Reform","Expanding our financial resources through transparent and effective public financial management.",""],[1,"24","1","Public Finance Management Strengthening","strengthening public finance management (PFM)",""],[1,"28","13","Public Financial Management Reform and Institutional Capacity Strengthening","Modernizing Myanmar's PFM systems while strengthening the capacity of relevant institutions will enable the efficient, accountable, transparent and responsive delivery of public services.",""],[1,"28","13","Public Financial Management Structure Review for Decentralized Governance","Furthermore, overall PFM structures will need to be revisited in order to reflect our country's drive towards a more decentralized system of governance in line with the vision of a democratic federal Union.",""],[1,"29","1","Public Financial Management Roadmap","Myanmar's PFM roadmap shall be ambitious yet attainable.",""],[1,"29","2","Public Financial Management Accountability and Transparency Reform","important steps will be taken to enhance external oversight and overall accountability of Myanmar's PFM system, including making significantly more budget information available to the general public and to integrating gender-responsive approaches amongst other measures.",""],[1,"29","5","Public Financial Management Strengthening","Strengthen public financial management to support stability and the efficient allocation of public resources",""],[1,"29","6","Budget Transparency Enhancement Measures","Significantly increase overall budget transparency, including the continued publication of Citizen Budgets, presentation of tax expenditures in annual budgets and other measures",""],[1,"29","8","Public Expenditure Review Recommendation Implementation","Implement recommendations of Public Expenditure Reviews",""],[1,"29","12","Budget Proposal Scrutiny and Expenditure Rationalization","Strengthen scrutiny and oversight of budget proposals and cut unnecessary expenditures",""],[1,"29","14","Public Financial Management Capacity Enhancement","Enhance the capacity of national and sub-national PFM, including provisions for nationally-led strategic infrastructure planning and investment and related revenue generation and asset management",""],[1,"30","1","Inclusive Public Participation in Budget Processes","Encourage greater and more inclusive public participation in budgetary processes at all levels",""],[1,"30","3","Gender Responsive Budgeting Integration","Integrate gender responsive budgeting at all levels to ensure the budget is adequately structured to address gender inequality",""],[1,"30","5","Revenue Sharing Mechanism for Extractives Revenues","Introduce revenue sharing mechanisms, including revenues generated from the extractives industry, to support more equitable allocation of tax revenues across all States and Regions",""]],"7":[[1,"24","5","Formalisation of Informal Remittance System","It is policy measures such as these, combined with other ambitious reforms such as formalising informal remittance system that will contribute to a significantly strengthened macroeconomic landscape.",""],[1,"25","16","Formalization of Informal Remittance Systems","Formalize hundi and similar informal remittance systems",""],[1,"40","17","Financial Sector Liberalisation","It is therefore imperative that the banking and financial services sector be further liberalised, and also that the capacity of the CBM be enhanced, particularly in","CBM"],[1,"41","1","Financial Sector Partnership Promotion","partnerships between domestic and foreign financial institutions will be encouraged in various forms, particularly those that enhance the capacity of our domestic banks to expand access to financial services.",""],[1,"41","1","Foreign Bank Branch Regulatory Relaxation","the MSDP seeks to relax conditions imposed on foreign bank branches, not only so that they can contribute to national capital formation, but also so that they contribute to making the interbank market more efficient.",""],[1,"41","1","State-Owned Bank Rehabilitation Reform","reform of Myanmar's remaining State-owned banks aims at rehabilitating institutions that can act as a bulwark against instability, while pursuing national and social goals beyond those amenable to private incentive.",""],[1,"41","6","Domestic Financial Institutions Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen the capacity of domestic financial institutions",""],[1,"41","10","Support for Non-Bank Financial Institutions","Strengthen and expand support to non-bank financial institutions",""],[1,"41","14","Expansion of Mobile and Fintech Services","Expand the scope of mobile and fin-tech services, including through both domestic and foreign financial actors",""],[1,"42","1","Banking Sector Liberalisation","Continue liberalisation of the banking sector including through plans and regulations for the Financial Institutions Law (FIL) and Foreign Exchange Management Law (FEML)",""],[1,"42","2","Financial Sector Legal and Regulatory Reform","The legal and regulatory environment enables financial institutions to manage and price risk, secure creditor rights and claims, and inclusively finance sustainable growth (PSD-AP, Pillar 2)",""],[1,"42","4","Bank Early Detection and Resolution Mechanism","Establish early detection and management mechanisms for weak banks, develop plans for bank recovery and resolution, and develop lender of last resort capabilities to contribute to increased financial sector stability",""],[1,"42","6","Comprehensive Microfinance Sector Strategy","Promote more inclusive access to finance by developing a comprehensive microfinance sector strategy with clear regulatory arrangements, including a tiered system that serves different objectives and is cognizant of barriers faced by women and ethnic groups",""],[1,"42","7","Microfinance Industry Strengthening","A strong microfinance industry led by well- managed MFIs which compete to provide payment, deposit, loan, and other financial products, and serve both microenterprises and SMEs in urban and rural areas (PSD-AP, Pillar 2)",""],[1,"42","9","Anti-Money Laundering and Counter-Terrorism Financing Strengthening","Strengthen the financial system against money laundering and the funding of terrorism and other nefarious activities",""],[1,"42","10","Legal and Regulatory Framework for Inclusive Sustainable Finance","The legal and regulatory environment enables financial institutions to manage and price risk, secure creditor rights and claims, and inclusively finance sustainable growth (PSD-AP, Pillar 2)",""],[1,"42","11","Bank Prudential Compliance Measures","Introduce measures that enable Myanmar banks to ensure full compliance with applicable prudential standards",""],[1,"43","1","Foreign Bank Market Access Liberalization","Increase ability of foreign banks to participate in domestic banking activities, including through continued liberalisation of market access and allowing foreign banks to take equity positions in domestic banks",""],[1,"43","3","State-Owned Bank Restructuring","Restructure State owned banks to ensure stability of the financial system, reduce fiscal risk and ensure a level playing field for all financial institutions",""],[1,"43","4","State-Owned Bank Restructuring and Liquidation","State-owned banks are restructured and/or liquidated, with remaining State FIs competing on equal terms with private FIs (PSD-AP, Pillar 2)",""],[1,"43","5","Legal and Financial Infrastructure for Inclusive Access to Finance","Improve the legal and financial infrastructure required to enhance greater and more inclusive access to finance",""],[1,"43","6","Legal and Regulatory Framework for Inclusive Sustainable Finance","The legal and regulatory environment enables financial institutions to manage and price risk, secure creditor rights and claims, and inclusively finance sustainable growth (PSD-AP, Pillar 2)",""],[1,"43","7","Central Bank Supervisory and Regulatory Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen the CBM's supervisory and regulatory capacity, including through the development of a comprehensive banking sector strategy with clear responsibilities for the CBM",""],[1,"43","13","Financial Transparency and Reporting Regulation Enforcement","Increase financial transparency, including by enforcing existing regulations on financial reporting and the introduction of additional transparency-related regulations for financial institutions",""],[1,"43","17","Insurance Sector Liberalization Reform","Strengthen and further liberalize the insurance sector",""],[1,"56","8","Cross-Border Financial Services for Migrant Workers","Provide improved cross- border financial services for migrant workers",""]],"8":[[1,"38","10","Review of Trade Institutional and Legal Framework","Myanmar will review its institutional and legal framework governing domestic and international trade and pursue a range of policies to facilitate trade and to diversify its exports.",""],[1,"38","10","Trade Facilitation and Export Diversification Policies","Myanmar will review its institutional and legal framework governing domestic and international trade and pursue a range of policies to facilitate trade and to diversify its exports.",""],[1,"38","11","Trade Connectivity and Customs Facilitation Reform","Myanmar will improve our connectivity with neighbouring countries and those further afield, by ensuring that relevant regulations and procedures are clear; that customs, trade and logistical services are improved; that more advanced IT and database systems are in place; that single-window one-stop centres are developed; and that customs single stop inspections (SSIs) are established in cooperation with neighbouring countries.",""],[1,"38","11","Formal Trade Sector Reform","Reform of the formal trade sector is also of particular importance in a country such as Myanmar, where a sizeable informal trade sector exists in parallel.",""],[1,"39","3","Priority Export Value Chain Strengthening and Linkage Building","Strengthen priority, pro-job creation export value chains and build linkages with foreign companies and buyers, aligned with the NES",""],[1,"39","5","Customs, Trade, and Logistics Efficiency and Transparency Reform","Improve the efficiency and transparency of customs, trade, and logistical services including by implementing relevant recommendations in the DTIS",""],[1,"39","8","Trade and Customs Procedure Guidelines","Publish clear guidelines on trade and customs procedures/regulations, including on the ASEAN National Trade Repository",""],[1,"39","9","Trade in Goods Market Access and Tariff Simplification Measures","Commitments made under ASEAN and WTO on trade in goods to benefit from accrued market access, simplified tariff structure and increased transparency (MTP-AFT, Pillar 1)",""],[1,"39","10","Tariff Rationalization for Trade Facilitation","Conduct tariff rationalization, including to support the ASEAN Trade in Goods Agreement (ATIGA)",""],[1,"39","11","Trade in Goods Market Access and Tariff Simplification Measures","Commitments made under ASEAN and WTO on trade in goods to benefit from accrued market access, simplified tariff structure and increased transparency (MTP-AFT, Pillar 1);",""],[1,"39","15","Trade-Related Legal and Institutional Reform","Narrow gaps in legislation, and review incentives, mandates and organizational structures of trade related public entities to facilitate increased trade",""],[1,"39","16","Trade-Related Institutional Capacity Restructuring","Design and implement a thorough reshaping of MoC and trade-related institutions organizational capabilities to respond effectively to the needs of reform (MTP-AFT Pillar 1)","MoC"],[1,"40","1","Trade and Customs Simplification Reform","Simplify trade and customs regulations and procedures, with effective use of MACCS, to reduce regulatory discretion, and reduce cost/time for customs clearance in line with sub-regional, regional, and international commitments",""],[1,"40","3","GMS Cross-Border Transport Facilitation Agreement Implementation","Implement the GMS Cross Border Transport Facilitation Agreement (CBTA)",""],[1,"40","5","Non-Tariff Measures Review and Reform","Review Non-Tariff Measures (NTM) and reform as needed, while ensuring the protection of workers, social norms, the environment, and public health",""],[1,"40","6","Regulatory Framework Transparency and Bottleneck Reduction Reform","Enhance the country's regulatory framework by increasing transparency, access to information and addressing legal and regulatory bottlenecks (MFT for AFT, Pillar 1)",""],[1,"40","8","Implementation of the ASEAN Economic Community 2025 Consolidated Strategic Action Plans","Continue implementing the ASEAN Economic Community (AEC) 2025 Consolidated Strategic Action Plans (CSAP)",""],[1,"40","9","Trade in Goods Market Access and Tariff Simplification Measures","Commitments made under ASEAN and WTO on trade in goods to benefit from accrued market access, simplified tariff structure and increased transparency (MTP-AFT, Pillar 1)",""],[1,"40","11","Comprehensive Trade Policy Development","Develop a comprehensive trade policy to provide the basis for efficient and effective trade negotiations at bilateral, regional and multilateral levels",""],[1,"40","14","National Quality Infrastructure Roadmap","Develop and implement National Quality Infrastructure Roadmap (both SPS and Non-SPS measures) which meets both service provision and trade facilitation need",""],[1,"40","15","Product Safety Standards Compliance and Export Competitiveness Enhancement","Ensure that our products meet required safety standards and enhance our competitiveness in exporting agricultural and other products.",""],[1,"46","6","Market Linkages and Competitiveness Enhancement","Enhanced Market Linkages and Competitiveness (AD SIP Outcome 3",""]],"9":[[1,"37","15","Special Economic Zone and Industrial Estate Development","Develop SEZ and industrial estates based on strategic planning that considers all economic, social and environmental aspects",""]],"10":[[1,"14","3","Intellectual Property Rights Technical Support System","Establishing technical systems and procedures to support intellectual property rights that can encourage innovation and the development of advanced technology.",""],[1,"32","5","Creativity and Innovation Promotion for the Digital Economy","the GoM will promote the role of creativity and innovation in manufacturing, industrial and service sectors, with an emphasis on preparing for the coming digital economy to further generate high quality jobs and induce structural transformation.",""],[1,"46","9","Creative Industries and Innovation Support Programme","the GoM will seek to support the development of our nation's creative industries, encourage innovation, research and development, entrepreneurship and creative disruption.",""],[1,"46","9","Education-to-Workplace Innovation Reform","Related reform initiatives must begin in the classroom and follow the individual into the workplace, leading to a more vibrant, innovative and competitive private and public sector.",""],[1,"46","13","Legal and Regulatory Framework Strengthening","Develop and strengthen relevant legal and regulatory frameworks in support of greater",""],[1,"46","14","Innovation Legal and Institutional Strengthening","Strengthen legal and institutional basis to promote innovation (EP11)",""],[1,"47","1","National Innovation Policy Development","including through the development of a National Innovation Policy",""],[1,"47","2","National Innovation and Creativity Ecosystem Development","Strengthen links between academia, research institutions and the private sector to develop a national innovation and creativity ecology",""],[1,"47","3","Innovation Legal and Institutional Strengthening","Strengthen legal and institutional basis to promote innovation (EP11)",""],[1,"47","5","Research and Development Financing Access Expansion","Increase access to financing for research and development",""],[1,"47","6","Innovation Legal and Institutional Framework Strengthening","Strengthen legal and institutional basis to promote innovation (EP11)",""],[1,"47","8","Local Entrepreneur Finance and Commercialization Support","Facilitate greater access to finance and the commercialization of products and services produced by local entrepreneurs and 'start- ups'",""],[1,"47","9","Innovation Legal and Institutional Strengthening","Strengthen legal and institutional basis to promote innovation (EP11)",""],[1,"47","12","Innovation and Scientific Research Support","Encourage and support innovation and scientific research in all sectors",""],[1,"47","13","Innovation Legal and Institutional Strengthening","Strengthen legal and institutional basis to promote innovation (EP11)",""],[1,"47","15","Intellectual Property Rights Strengthening and Patent and Trademark Office Establishment","Strengthen intellectual property rights, including through a Myanmar patent and trademark office to protect innovations and inventions",""],[1,"47","16","Innovation Legal and Institutional Strengthening","Strengthen legal and institutional basis to promote innovation (EP11)",""],[1,"47","18","Inclusive Digital Economy Transition","Enable our transition toward an inclusive digital economy, expanding connectivity and access to online services, supporting innovation and data literacy while ensuring security and online privacy",""],[1,"47","19","Legal and Institutional Framework for Innovation Promotion","Strengthen legal and institutional basis to promote innovation (EP11)",""]],"11":[[1,"13","12","Balanced Agriculture and Industry Development Model","Establishing an economic model that balances agriculture and industry and supports the holistic development of the agriculture, livestock and industrial sectors, so as to enable rounded development, food security and increased exports.",""],[1,"33","7","Agriculture, Aquaculture, and Food Sector Education and Training Reform","Revise and develop education and training in the agriculture, aquaculture and food sectors, responding to the evolving needs of farmers and the rural private sector",""],[1,"33","12","Agricultural Investment and Mechanization Market Enablement","Create market conditions to enable greater investment in agriculture, aquaculture and polyculture, and mechanization",""],[1,"34","1","Market Intelligence and Data Access Improvement","Improve access to market intelligence and other key data to support more informed producer and consumer decision making",""],[1,"34","3","Market and Logistics Infrastructure Development for Agricultural Value Chains","Develop market and logistics infrastructure to support agricultural, aquacultural and polycultural productivity and value chain enhancement",""],[1,"34","6","Agricultural Investment Regulation Reform","Improve investment regulations for agri- investors, including through facilitating foreign investor access to the agriculture, aquaculture and polyculture sectors",""],[1,"34","14","Enabling Environment for Farmer Production and Trade","Facilitate an enabling environment which enables farmers to grow, produce, and trade freely",""],[1,"34","18","Rural Financial Products and Risk Management Regulatory Reform","Improve the regulatory environment such that it facilitates the development of financial products, and risk management tools and strategies that respond to the unique requirements of rural populations",""],[1,"35","1","Context-Responsive Agricultural Development Planning","Develop agricultural development plans responsive to specific contexts and needs at all levels",""],[1,"35","7","Private Sector Business Freedom and Production Diversification Incentives","Enable private sector actors to freely choose and manage their businesses while providing incentives for producers to intensify and diversify production to optimize returns",""]],"12":[[1,"33","9","Irrigation and Drainage Service Enhancement","Enhance irrigation and drainage services, and support more efficient and sustainable water management systems",""],[1,"34","10","Climate-Resilient Rural Infrastructure Development","Lessen rural communities' exposure to extreme climate-related events, especially in disaster prone areas including supporting the development of climate-resilient rural infrastructure",""],[1,"55","7","Climate-Resilient Crop Cultivation Promotion","Promote the cultivation of crops resistant to pests, droughts and floods",""],[1,"60","4","Climate-Resilient and Climate-Smart Agricultural Practices Promotion","Climate-resilient productivity and climate- smart responses promoted in the agriculture, fisheries and livestock sectors while also promoting resource- efficient and low-carbon practices",""],[1,"60","6","Climate-Resilient and Climate-Smart Adaptation Technologies Adoption","Adopt climate-resilient and environmentally sound adaptation technologies and climate-smart management practices in all sectors",""],[1,"60","7","Climate-Resilient and Climate-Smart Agricultural Practices Promotion","Climate-resilient productivity and climate- smart responses promoted in the agriculture, fisheries and livestock sectors while also promoting resource- efficient and low-carbon practices",""]],"13":[[1,"33","14","Rural Land Tenure and Property Rights Strengthening","Strengthen rural households' land tenure, property rights and related enforcement capacities",""],[1,"34","8","Locally Generated Rural Development Initiatives","Enable and empower rural communities to initiate locally-generated, inclusive and consultative development initiatives",""]],"14":[[1,"13","9","Vocational Education and Training Expansion","improving and expanding vocational education and training.",""],[1,"35","13","Workplace Safety and Non-Discrimination Regulatory Reform","Introduce and enforce regulations and protections related to workplace safety, inclusivity and non- discrimination in all forms, and the practice of equal pay for work of equal value",""],[1,"36","2","Support for Inclusive Business and Labour Representative Organizations","Support the emergence of inclusive business and trade associations, representative employers' organisations and trade unions",""],[1,"53","17","Minimum Wage Enforcement and Monitoring Mechanism","Enforce the minimum wage together with monitoring mechanisms that track both application and impact",""],[1,"55","18","Workplace Rights Protection and Anti-Discrimination Measures","Myanmar shall focus on actions that will ensure our nation's places of work are safe from the indignity of oppression, discrimination and harassment, with particular attention placed upon protecting the rights of women, children and migrant workers, each deserving special and particular protection and support.",""],[1,"55","18","Worker Skills and Mobility Development Support","In doing so, Myanmar shall ensure that all workers are provided with opportunities to develop the skills and experience necessary to support their social and economic mobility, allowing them to fully contribute to the nation's development with dignity and respect.",""],[1,"56","14","Labour Rights Protection and Workplace Safety Initiative","Protect labour rights and promote safe and secure working environments for all workers, including migrant workers",""]],"15":[[1,"15","4","Peace and National Reconciliation Strategy","this MSDP formulates specific strategies for peace and national reconciliation for Myanmar",""],[1,"16","2","Inclusive Political Dialogue Framework for Peace Process","Myanmar has initiated an inclusive framework for political dialogue so that all the stakeholders in the peace process can move towards building a common vision of a democratic federal Union.",""],[1,"16","2","Expansion of Political Dialogue for Union Peace Accord","The continuation and expansion of this political dialogue will facilitate the process for securing a Union Peace Accord so that dividends of peace can be shared and enjoyed by everyone affected by more than 60 years of debilitating conflict.",""],[1,"16","5","Inclusive Peace Process Participation Action Plans","These Action Plans place a particular significance on ensuring meaningful involvement in the peace process by those rendered most vulnerable by conflict, including but not limited to those displaced by conflict, women and youth.",""],[1,"16","9","Union Peace Conference Sessions","Hold further sessions of the Union Peace Conference: 21st Century Panglong",""],[1,"16","12","Inclusive Political Dialogue Process","Conduct inclusive political dialogues with all relevant stakeholders at national and sub-national levels",""],[1,"17","1","Inclusive Peace Process Expansion","Further integrate NCA non- signatory EAOs into peace processes and work toward their signing of the NCA, and expand participation of other relevant stakeholders, with clear roles and responsibilities for all",""],[1,"17","7","Women’s Participation in Political Dialogues Initiative","Strive for at least 30% participation of women in political dialogues",""],[1,"17","10","Political Dialogue on Union Principles","Based on the outcome of political dialogues, agree key principles for the establishment of a Union founded upon democracy and federalism",""],[1,"17","13","National Ceasefire Agreement Implementation","Implement and follow the articles in the NCA",""]],"16":[[1,"17","17","Fiscal Federalism Implementation","the key tenets of fiscal federalism related to both equalisation payments and fiscal transfers to Myanmar's States and Regions, as well as decentralisation of natural resources management - are fully implemented under the umbrella of the MSDP and within the scope of the Constitution.",""],[1,"17","18","Cooperative Basic Infrastructure and Service Delivery Expansion","the provision of basic infrastructure, services delivery and connectivity are undertaken with enhanced cooperation with existing, ethnic-affiliated service providers and local communities",""],[1,"17","18","Community Consultation and Feedback Mechanism for Social Cohesion","social cohesion can be strengthened through the consultation and full engagement with ethnic leaders and communities, reinforced by the use of transparent and accountable community feedback mechanisms",""],[1,"18","2","Conflict-Sensitive Socio-Economic Development Approach","ensuring conflict-sensitive approaches to socio-economic development, with a focus on those most vulnerable and furthest behind, will contribute to the active management and mitigation of the risk of exacerbating inequalities or doing harm.",""],[1,"18","2","Inclusive Livelihood Options and Access Expansion","It will also contribute to the creation of innovative, and contextually appropriate livelihood options that can then be further enhanced by broadening access to finance, markets, technology and information.",""],[1,"18","6","Decentralized Development Management and IDP Resettlement Planning","Decentralize management of development activities, particularly in post-conflict and conflict-affected areas, as a means of fostering greater social cohesion, including the development of IDP resettlement plans that facilitate safe, voluntary, and dignified returns",""],[1,"18","9","Sub-national Socio-Economic Development Planning and Resource Mobilisation","Develop and implement sub-national socio- economic development plans and plans for resource mobilisation",""],[1,"18","15","Regional Connectivity Strengthening","Strengthen social, economic and physical connectivity in lagging regions with growth/population hubs within Myanmar and regions beyond",""],[1,"19","3","Implementation of the Advisory Commission on Rakhine State Recommendations","Fully implement recommendations set forth within the Final Report of the Advisory Commission on Rakhine State",""],[1,"19","6","Implementation of Investigatory Commission Recommendations","Fully implement recommendations drawn from the Maungdaw Region Investigation Commission and those of other relevant military/security-related investigatory bodies",""],[1,"19","9","Prioritization of Development Assistance and Investment to Conflict-Affected Areas","Prioritize flows of development assistance and investment into conflict-affected States and Regions",""],[1,"20","2","Rule of Law Expansion to Conflict-Affected Areas","concrete steps be taken to bring the rule of law to conflict-affected areas",""]],"17":[[1,"19","12","Legal Transparency and Consultative Legislation Reform","the MSDP seeks to make the law more transparent and consultative, producing legislation that is in the interest of all our people, administered fairly and impartially, with respect for human rights, and without discrimination so that no person is above the law and every person may benefit equally from its administration.",""],[1,"19","13","Community-Level Rule of Law Strengthening","Steps must also be taken to strengthen the rule of law at the community level so that people's life chances are not diminished by injustice.",""],[1,"19","14","Law Enforcement Capacity Strengthening for Personal Security","Steps will also be taken to strengthen the abilities of law enforcement institutions to deliver personal security, particularly for vulnerable groups, using new and innovative approaches such as community policing and other cross-border collaborations.",""],[1,"20","6","Contract and Legislation Review and Enforcement Improvement","Improve efficiency and effectiveness in reviewing, vetting, drafting, implementing and enforcing contracts and legislation",""],[1,"20","8","Legal Aid Policy Development and Coverage Expansion","Review the current legal aid system and develop a legal aid policy that expands coverage of eligible beneficiaries",""],[1,"20","10","Fair Trial Standards in Criminal Prosecutions","Strengthen adherence to fair trial standards during criminal prosecutions",""],[1,"20","12","Justice and Rule of Law Access Improvement","Ensure greater understanding of and access to justice and the rule of law, including individual rights, due process and legal services",""],[1,"20","14","Bar Council Act Reform","Develop a robust and independent bar, including by reforming the Bar Council Act",""],[1,"20","16","Judiciary and Justice Sector Institutional Strengthening","Enhance independence, effectiveness and administrative capacity of the judiciary and justice sector institutions, while ensuring professionalism, accountability and integrity",""],[1,"20","18","Comprehensive Justice Sector Reform Strategy","Develop a comprehensive justice sector reform strategy",""],[1,"37","7","Dispute Resolution System Enhancement","Enhance systems for dispute resolution, such as the use of ombudsmen and alternative dispute mechanisms",""],[1,"37","8","Legal Implementation and Dispute Resolution Strengthening","Improved implementation and enforcement of laws and better dispute resolution mechanisms (PSD-AP Pillar 1)",""],[1,"38","6","Commercial Law Framework Strengthening","Strengthen the quality of our commercial law framework, ensuring the application of effective and efficient commercial rule of law and commercial dispute resolution mechanisms",""]],"18":[[1,"21","1","Government Machinery Strengthening and Institutional Capacity Development","Realising the full implementation of this MSDP, while at the same time achieving high levels of administrative and institutional performance, will only be possible by strengthening the machinery of government at all levels, together with the instalment of transparent and accountable systems that support effective service delivery.",""],[1,"21","1","Evidence-Based Policy Development and Governance Mechanisms","The GoM recognises that improving policy development that is rooted in strong evidence, enhancing its implementation through improved governance mechanisms, and strengthening institutional performance management and monitoring systems are all key elements which underpin good governance, and must form a central platform upon which any long-term development process is based.",""],[1,"21","1","Regulatory Modernisation and Delegation of Authority Reform","Therefore, institutional capacity development will be bolstered by renewed, modernised and clear regulations, policies and procedures and a more effective delegation of authority.",""],[1,"21","2","Civil Service Human Capacity Development Investment","Institutional capacity development will also be bolstered by a strong investment in civil service human capacity development.",""],[1,"21","2","Public Sector Management Reform","The MSDP includes a strong emphasis on modernising the public service and the introduction of new public-sector management practices.",""],[1,"21","6","Civil Service Regulatory and Compensation Reform","Continually review, standardize and upgrade as needed civil service regulations, procedures, codes of conduct, compensation and allowances to create new, innovative and inclusive pathways toward public sector employment and career advancement",""],[1,"22","1","Parliamentary Oversight Strengthening for Budget, Planning, and Audit Processes","Increase public sector transparency and accountability by enhancing parliamentary oversight as part of standard budget, planning and audit processes",""],[1,"22","5","Legislative Review and Government Reform Initiative","Continually review, standardize and upgrade relevant legislation and undertake new initiatives which will facilitate more effective, accountable and transparent government",""]],"19":[[1,"13","10","National Data ID Card System","Prioritising the rapid development of fundamental economic infrastructure, such as electricity generation, roads and ports, and establishing a data ID card system, a digital government strategy, and an e-government system.",""],[1,"13","10","Digital Government Strategy and E-Government System","Prioritising the rapid development of fundamental economic infrastructure, such as electricity generation, roads and ports, and establishing a data ID card system, a digital government strategy, and an e-government system.",""],[1,"21","2","E-Government and Public Service Modernisation Programme","Institutional performance will be further enhanced with the introduction of e-government platforms and the use of online applications for information sharing, decision-making and approvals.",""],[1,"22","3","Digital Online Government Services Expansion","Bring public sector services delivery closer to communities through the use of G2B and G2C digital online government services",""],[1,"45","3","Priority Infrastructure Development and E-Government Introduction","Accelerated development of priority infrastructures and introduction of e- government (EP 4)",""],[1,"45","9","E-Government Introduction","Accelerated development of priority infrastructures and introduction of e- government (EP 4)",""],[1,"45","15","Priority Infrastructure Development and E-Government Introduction","Accelerated development of priority infrastructures and introduction of e- government (EP 4)",""],[1,"45","18","Priority Infrastructure Development and E-Government Introduction","Accelerated development of priority infrastructures and introduction of e- government (EP 4)",""],[1,"45","20","Priority Infrastructure Development and E-Government Introduction","Accelerated development of priority infrastructures and introduction of e- government (EP4)",""],[1,"46","2","Priority Infrastructure Development and E-Government Introduction","Accelerated development of priority infrastructures and introduction of e- government (EP4)",""],[1,"46","6","Priority Infrastructure Development and E-Government Introduction","Accelerated development of priority infrastructures and introduction of e- government (EP4);",""],[1,"46","8","Priority Infrastructure Development and E-Government Introduction","Accelerated development of priority infrastructures and introduction of e- government (EP4)",""]],"20":[[1,"21","2","Public Sector Transparency and Accountability Initiative","Transparency, accountability and integrity shall likewise serve as pinnacle elements of this drive towards improved institutional performance.",""],[1,"22","7","Anti-Corruption Legal and Enforcement Strengthening","Review and strengthen anti-corruption related legislation, enforcement measures and policies, including strengthening grievance and whistle- blower mechanisms",""],[1,"22","9","Public Engagement and Government Communication Enhancement","Hence, it is imperative that enhanced engagement and greater understanding be facilitated through the use of modern communication strategies and technologies (including electronic means), across all levels of the government, within and between ethnic nationalities, and all other stakeholders.",""],[1,"22","13","Civic Engagement and Public Consultation Strengthening","Strengthen civic engagement and public consultation processes",""],[1,"23","2","Public Sector Communications Capacity Strengthening","Strengthen public sector communications capacities, allowing for more effective policy dialogue and feedback mechanisms to emerge",""],[1,"23","4","Citizens' Access to Information and Public Information Transparency Reform","Improve and legalize citizens' access to information and broaden the accessibility of information on budgets, legislation, strategies plans, policies, statistics and other key information held by public authorities",""],[1,"23","6","Inclusive Participatory Planning Practices","Strengthen inclusive planning practices based on participatory processes across all levels of government",""],[1,"23","8","Cultural and Linguistic Pluralism Promotion and Freedom of Expression Legislation","Promote cultural and linguistic pluralism at all levels with legislation protecting the freedom of expression for individuals and groups",""],[1,"23","10","Public Procurement Tendering Reform","Establish a standardized, transparent and competitive tendering system for public procurement at both national and sub-national levels",""]],"21":[[1,"4","1","National Sustainable Development Strategy","The MSDP delivers this strategy, providing an overall framework for coordination and cooperation across all ministries, and all States and Regions to forge a common path towards the emergence of a prosperous, peaceful and democratic Myanmar.",""],[1,"4","2","MSDP Strategic Project Review Process","major project proposals from all line ministries and States and Regions shall be reviewed based upon their strategic alignment with the MSDP.",""],[1,"4","2","Project Bank for Coordinated Project Implementation","A Project Bank shall also be created to facilitate the effective, coordinated and transparent implementation of these projects.",""],[1,"4","3","Sustainable National Planning and Project Prioritization","Moving forward, national planning, including the implementation of existing projects, shall place a special focus on development sustainability and harmonious coordination.",""],[1,"9","7","Whole-of-Government Development Framework","the MSDP is intended to provide a whole-of-government development framework that offers coherence to these existing strategic documents, ensuring that they are executed in ways that are consistent with macro-level national development priorities.",""],[1,"9","7","MSDP Action Plan Alignment with SDG Targets","the MSDP mediates between local developmental needs and global sustainable development agenda by aligning MSDP action plans with global SDG targets.",""],[1,"10","1","Mainstream Youth, Gender Empowerment, Equity and Inclusion Across MSDP Implementation","issues pertaining to youth, gender empowerment, equity and inclusion shall be considered cross-cutting, to be mainstreamed into all aspects of MSDP implementation.",""],[1,"10","5","SDG Mainstreaming Across MSDP Implementation","sustainability in all its forms shall be considered cross-cutting, to be mainstreamed into all aspects of MSDP implementation.",""],[1,"10","6","Conflict-Sensitive Mainstreaming Across MSDP Implementation","it is essential that all initiatives are designed, implemented, managed and monitored with the participation of all stakeholders in a conflict-sensitive manner.",""],[1,"44","2","Public Investment Project Bank","A Project Bank of public investments required to implement the MSDP shall provide a list of prioritized projects, particularly infrastructure projects, for public consumption so that the flow of development assistance, the allocation of the budget, and the participation of private sector can be strategically aligned with the goals and strategies contained within this MSDP.",""],[1,"44","3","Strategic Public Financing for Priority Projects","Other priority projects with a clear social and economic development impact will be financed by the government's budget or through the targeted and strategic use of other sources of development finance, including development assistance.",""],[1,"45","8","Project Bank for Public Investment Programs","Develop a Project Bank of Public Investment Programs (PIPs)",""]],"22":[[1,"48","13","Equitable Access and Quality Improvement in Education","the GoM is determined to promote more equitable access and higher quality outcomes for students",""],[1,"48","13","Safe and Inclusive School Improvement","Doing so will mean ensuring our schools are safe and cater to the needs of all",""],[1,"48","13","Early Childhood Education Investment","investing in early childhood education during the students' most formative years",""],[1,"48","13","Basic Education Structural Reform","broad-ranging structural reforms are required in order to ensure that basic education not only delivers literacy and numeracy, but also contributes to students' overall development in ways that allow them to realise their full potential",""],[1,"49","4","National Curriculum Development for 21st Century Skills","Develop a comprehensive national curriculum which will provide our youth with 21st century skillsets to enable them to serve the nation as drivers of a competitive, innovative and creative economy",""],[1,"49","7","Protection of Young People in Educational Environments","Eliminate abuse, discrimination, and exploitation faced by young people, including girls and other vulnerable groups, in all educational environments",""],[1,"49","9","Basic Education Infrastructure and Accessibility Expansion","Expand access to both the hard and soft infrastructure necessary to enable access to a comprehensive, quality, free basic education, ensuring provision of gender and disability-sensitive school facilities, technologies, including water and sanitation services",""],[1,"49","12","Teacher Recruitment, Training, and Quality Assurance Strengthening","Strengthen the quality of teacher recruitment, training, academic administration and quality assurance measures at all levels and in all forms",""],[1,"49","13","Quality Assessment System for Student Learning","Teachers and education managers implement a quality assessment system to improve student learning outcomes",""],[1,"50","7","Multilingual and Ethnic-Language Basic Education Access Improvement","Improve access to quality basic education, including through the use of multilingual and ethnic- language based content",""],[1,"50","9","Alternative and Out-of-School Education Expansion and Quality Improvement","Expand access to and improve quality of alternative and out-of- school education services",""],[1,"50","11","Preschool and Kindergarten Access and Quality Improvement","Expand access to and improve quality of preschool and kindergarten services",""],[1,"53","4","School Dropout Prevention and Child Labour Reduction Measures","Introduce measures to prevent school dropout and combat the use of child labour",""],[1,"53","9","Back-to-School and Vocational Training Support for Working Children","Provide back to school programmes for working children and/or vocational training school assistance until they reach the legal age for work",""]],"23":[[1,"48","13","Demand-Driven TVET and Tertiary Education Expansion","further effort is required to strengthen career-relevant education streams, including demand-driven TVET courses and quality tertiary education opportunities",""],[1,"49","14","TVET Curriculum Modernization","Develop comprehensive 21st century-ready TVET curricula that meets current and future private sector needs",""],[1,"50","1","Expanded Access to TVET for Underrepresented Groups","Enable greater access to TVET for target and underrepresented groups, including disadvantaged population groups and people living with disabilities",""],[1,"50","2","TVET Access and Quality Assurance Reform","More learners can access TVET and graduate from quality-assured and labour market-responsive TVET programmes under a more effective TVET management system",""],[1,"50","5","Higher Education Quality and Access Improvement","Improve the quality of and access to higher education through improved teacher training and academic administration",""],[1,"53","15","Vocational Education and Training Programmes for Poor Populations","Introduce vocational education and training programmes for poor populations",""]],"24":[[1,"2","28","Pro-Poor Universal Health Care Service Strengthening","Strategy 4.2: Strengthen health services systems enabling the provision of universal health care using a path that is explicitly pro-poor.",""],[1,"51","2","Pro-Poor Universal Health Services Strengthening","Strengthen health services systems enabling the provision of universal path that is explicitly pro-poor",""],[1,"51","3","Essential Package of Health Services Definition","Define a set of essential services and interventions to be included in an essential package of health services (EPHS), an intermediate package, and a comprehensive package",""],[1,"51","5","Equitable Health Investment Prioritization System","Establish a transparent system to prioritize health investments equitably and free from all forms of discrimination",""],[1,"51","7","Inclusive Township Health Plans Development","Develop Inclusive Township Health Plans (ITHP) supported by national templates and guidelines",""],[1,"51","10","Standard Treatment Guidelines Development and Periodic Review","Develop and update standard treatment guidelines with a process for periodic review and improvement",""],[1,"51","12","Health Workforce Production, Recruitment, and Deployment Reform","Improve links between the production, recruitment and deployment of our health workforce, including through gradually decentralizing decision- making to States and Regions.",""],[1,"51","14","Health Worker Training and Accreditation System","Strengthen health worker training, including through an accreditation system, to provide skills required for the delivery of basic health services",""],[1,"51","16","Family Planning and Sexual and Reproductive Health Services Expansion","Enhance availability and awareness of family planning, and ensure access to comprehensive sexual and reproductive education and healthcare services",""],[1,"57","5","National Investment Plan for Rural Water Supply, Sanitation and Hygiene in Schools and WASH in Health Facilities","National Investment Plan for Rural Water Supply, Sanitation and Hygiene in Schools and WASH in Health Facilities 2016-2030",""]],"25":[[1,"52","1","Communicable Disease Control and Epidemic Response","Control and combat epidemics such as HIV/AIDS, tuberculosis, malaria and neglected tropical diseases, hepatitis, water-borne diseases and other communicable diseases",""],[1,"53","6","Substance Harm Awareness and Education Programs","Strengthen awareness and educational programs related to the harmful use of drugs, alcohol, tobacco, and other commonly consumed carcinogens",""],[1,"55","16","Food and Food-Borne Disease Surveillance Enhancement","Enhance food and food-borne disease surveillance",""]],"26":[[1,"9","2","Comprehensive Poverty Reduction Strategy","The GoM is committed to mitigating poverty throughout the country, and has developed comprehensive strategies to address the issue, beyond simply stimulating economic growth.",""],[1,"52","5","Expansion of the Social Safety Net and Protection Services","expanding and deepening these programmes throughout the individual's life-cycle will ensure that a package of standard protections is accessible to all citizens.",""],[1,"52","10","Universal Cash Allowance Expansion for Pregnant Women and Young Children","Expand the universal cash allowance to all pregnant women and children up to age 2",""],[1,"52","13","Cash Allowances for People with Disabilities","Ensure implementation of cash allowances for people with disabilities",""],[1,"52","15","Universal Child Cash Allowance","Introduce universal cash allowances for children above 3",""],[1,"53","12","Public Employment Opportunities for Poor Populations","Introduce public employment opportunities for poor populations",""],[1,"53","19","Incapacity and Unemployment Benefits","Introduce incapacity and unemployment benefits",""],[1,"53","21","Universal Old-Age Cash Benefit","Provide universal cash benefits to people of older age",""],[1,"54","1","Expansion of Social Protection and Public Employment Programmes","Scale up existing social protection schemes and public employment programmes to mitigate the impact of and better manage responses to natural and man-made disasters and other shocks",""],[1,"54","4","Link Public Employment Programmes to Disaster Risk Management","Link public employment programmes to disaster risk management where feasible/appropriate",""]],"27":[[1,"34","16","Food Safety Standards Improvement","Improve food safety standards to protect human health and extract greater value from agricultural, aquacultural, livestock and related exports",""],[1,"52","18","Expansion of School Feeding Programmes","Expand school feeding programmes to all government schools",""],[1,"54","8","Household Food Security and Nutrition Improvement","Myanmar shall seek to enhance household-level food security by tackling the root causes of food insecurity and under-nutrition, while supporting healthy dietary practices.",""],[1,"54","8","Safe and Efficient Food Production Support","Myanmar will prioritise safe and efficient food production, particularly where chronic and acute food insecurity persists, while recognising that the natural environment - fertile soil, clean water and pollination - provides the very foundation of food production.",""],[1,"54","12","National Action Plan for Food and Nutrition","Develop comprehensive national strategies and actions plans to increase secure access to quality food, including a National Action Plan for Food and Nutrition and a National Strategy on Micronutrient Fortification and other relevant guidelines",""],[1,"54","12","National Strategy on Micronutrient Fortification","Develop comprehensive national strategies and actions plans to increase secure access to quality food, including a National Action Plan for Food and Nutrition and a National Strategy on Micronutrient Fortification and other relevant guidelines",""],[1,"54","12","Food Security Guidelines Development","Develop comprehensive national strategies and actions plans to increase secure access to quality food, including a National Action Plan for Food and Nutrition and a National Strategy on Micronutrient Fortification and other relevant guidelines",""],[1,"55","1","Comprehensive Acute Malnutrition Response","Develop comprehensive approaches to acute malnutrition, including emergency feeding",""],[1,"55","4","Nutrition Education and Healthy Food Awareness Programme","Enhance nutrition education and communication, including guidelines and awareness raising regarding healthy food related practices",""],[1,"55","9","Emergency Food Reserve Planning","Develop plans for emergency food reserves at different levels",""],[1,"55","12","Farmer Seed Utilization Knowledge Program","Empower farmers with knowledge regarding proper seed utilization, including the importance of not mixing varieties and types of seeds",""]],"28":[[1,"9","3","Safe and Affordable Migration Channels Development","the GoM also strives to develop legal, convenient, affordable and secure channels of migration from which not only migrants themselves, but also their left-behind families and communities, will benefit.",""],[1,"13","11","Employment Creation for Returning Migrants and Citizens","Creating employment opportunities for all citizens including those returning from abroad and giving greater priority in the short term to economic enterprises that create many job opportunities.",""],[1,"53","1","Human Trafficking Prevention and Punishment Programme","Introduce programmes and services to prevent and punish human trafficking",""],[1,"55","19","Migrant Engagement and Protection Initiative","this MSDP also emphasizes the need to harness the expertise, financial resources and energies of migrants for the development of the country while ensuring their safety and rights both domestically and internationally.",""],[1,"56","4","Universal Legal Identity and Birth Registration","Provide a legal identity for all, including birth registration",""],[1,"56","6","Legal, Affordable and Secure Migration Services","Promote legal, affordable and secure migration services",""],[1,"56","11","Diaspora Contribution Promotion Measures","Develop measures to encourage our diaspora's contribution to our domestic economy",""]],"29":[[1,"10","2","Mainstream Environmental Considerations into Policies and Projects","Therefore, the GoM is committed to a national development framework that enshrines the notion of environmental sustainability for future generations by systematically incorporating environmental considerations into the design and the implementation of its policies and projects.",""],[1,"14","1","Environmentally Sustainable Cities and Public Services Upgrade","Building environmentally sustainable cities, upgrading public services and utilities, expanding public spaces, and making greater efforts to protect and conserve our cultural heritage.",""],[1,"45","14","Social and Environmental Safeguards for Infrastructure Development","Establish and implement effective social and environmental safeguards against negative impacts of infrastructure development",""],[1,"56","17","Environmental Protection and Ecosystem Management Framework","Goal 5 focuses on the legal, institutional and policy frameworks required to better protect and manage our natural environment and ecosystems, through strengthened conservation efforts, improved development and infrastructure planning, and increased enforcement against illegal natural resource related practices, pollution and other harmful activities.",""],[1,"56","18","Sustainable Urban Development Mainstreaming","promoting sustainable urban development and the mainstreaming of environmental consideration into policies, plans and national accounting systems.",""],[1,"57","7","Mainstream Environmental and Biodiversity Protection in Planning","Myanmar will mainstream the protection of our environmental and biodiversity dividend into all manner of planning and decision making.",""],[1,"57","7","Environmental Safeguards and Enforcement Mechanisms","Whether on land, above ground or under water, a range of policy safeguards, legal protections and enforcement mechanisms will be deployed to ensure that unsuitable and destructive practices are phased out and replaced with more environmentally conscious approaches.",""],[1,"57","7","Inclusive Decision-Making for Vulnerable Communities","Myanmar will also ensure that individuals and communities, including those most vulnerable, are included in decision-making processes at all levels.",""],[1,"57","11","Environmental Awareness and Conservation Integration","Promote broad based environmental awareness, with a focus on integrating conservation practices into development and planning processes at all levels, including national accounting and reporting systems",""],[1,"59","9","Strategic Infrastructure Planning","Strategic infrastructure planning that takes into consideration social, environmental and economic costs and benefits will be necessary to ensure that the country can reap the greatest possible benefit from infrastructure development.",""]],"30":[[1,"55","14","Conservation Facilities for Genetic Resources and Species Classification","Develop conservation facilities to secure plant and animal genetic resources for food and agriculture related research, and classify local species, including those at risk of extinction",""],[1,"57","12","Biodiversity Mainstreaming Across Government and Society","Underlying causes of biodiversity loss are addressed through mainstreaming biodiversity across government and society",""],[1,"57","15","Biodiversity Mainstreaming Across Government and Society","Underlying causes of biodiversity loss are addressed through mainstreaming biodiversity across government and society",""],[1,"58","1","Sustainable Natural Resource Production and Consumption Plans","Implement plans at all levels to promote the sustainable production, consumption and use of our natural resources",""],[1,"58","4","Sustainable Land Use Management and Habitat Restoration","Reduce loss of, and restore degraded, natural habitats, through sustained, well- resourced land use management and take action against those committing unlawful environmental damage",""],[1,"58","7","Land Use Monitoring System Improvement","Improve land use monitoring systems in order to better inform sustainable policy and planning",""],[1,"58","12","Integrated Natural Resource Conservation and Protected Area Management","Conserve and protect terrestrial and inland water areas, coastal and marine areas, and national sanctuaries through integrated resources planning and effective and equitable management",""],[1,"58","15","Environmental Regulation Monitoring and Enforcement","Strengthen monitoring and enforcement of environmental regulations and take serious action against environmental crimes such as the illegal trade, poaching and trafficking of protected flora and fauna",""],[1,"58","17","Updated National Biodiversity Strategy and Action Plans","Implement an updated National Biodiversity Strategy and associated action plans",""],[1,"58","18","Participatory Planning, Knowledge Management, and Capacity Building","Enhanced implementation through participatory planning, knowledge management, and capacity building",""],[1,"58","22","Regulatory and Notification Strengthening","Introduce and strengthen regulation and notifications",""],[1,"59","3","Ecosystem Restoration and Safeguarding Initiative","Restore and safeguard ecosystems that provide essential services to local communities taking into account gender and the needs of youth, ethnic and local communities, the poor and other cultural considerations",""],[1,"59","6","Alternative Livelihoods Support for Environmental Conservation","Ensure access to alternative livelihoods for local populations as a strategy to ensure environmental protection and conservation",""],[1,"59","10","Community-Based Natural Resource Management Initiative","and will work with individuals and communities at all levels to improve natural resource management and mitigate, potentially even reverse, the impacts of climate change.",""],[1,"60","10","Natural Resource Management System for Biodiversity Resilience","Natural resource management system adopted that enhances the resilience of biodiversity and ecosystem services to support social and economic development and deliver carbon sequestration",""]],"31":[[1,"56","17","Green Investment and Renewable Energy Promotion Measures","Strategies and Action Plans involve encouraging good water use practices, increasing renewable energy generation, climate change mitigation, increasing green investments, protecting biodiversity, improving waste management,",""],[1,"57","14","Reform Harmful Subsidies and Introduce Positive Conservation Incentives","Revise and address, eliminate, phase out, or reform incentives, including subsidies, that are harmful to our natural assets, and introduce positive incentives that promote conservation and sustainability",""],[1,"59","8","Low-Carbon Green Economy Development Trajectory","Therefore, Myanmar will embark upon a low-carbon, green economy development trajectory that prioritises the efficient use of natural resources.",""],[1,"59","10","Climate-Sensitive Legal and Planning Integration","Myanmar will also integrate climate-sensitive approaches to existing laws and planning processes",""],[1,"60","2","Climate Resilience and Low-Carbon Transition Strategy","Increase climate change resilience, reduce exposure to disasters and livelihoods, and facilitate a shift to a low-carbon growth pathway",""],[1,"60","3","Mainstream Disaster Risk Reduction and Climate Mitigation Across Sectors","Integrate disaster risk reduction and climate change mitigation measures in policies, planning and budgeting procedures for all sectors",""],[1,"60","9","Climate Change Mainstreaming in Environmental and Natural Resource Management","Incorporate climate change dimensions into environmental and natural resource management policies, rules and regulations",""],[1,"60","12","Climate-Resilient and Low-Carbon Infrastructure Adaptation","Adapt infrastructure systems, including transport systems, to mitigate against heightened risks of natural disasters and new climatic conditions, while facilitating a transition to more efficient, low-carbon technologies",""],[1,"60","14","Industrial System Productivity and Competitiveness Enhancement","Increase the productivity and competitiveness of industrial systems through disaster and climate resilience, and low-carbon and green characteristics",""]],"32":[[1,"8","6","Public-Private Partnership Infrastructure Delivery","many infrastructure projects are being developed through various Public-Private Partnership (PPP) mechanisms to facilitate this",""],[1,"13","10","Fundamental Economic Infrastructure Development","Prioritising the rapid development of fundamental economic infrastructure, such as electricity generation, roads and ports, and establishing a data ID card system, a digital government strategy, and an e-government system.",""],[1,"44","1","Targeted Infrastructure Development and Financing Diversification","The GoM will focus on targeted infrastructure development with the aim of maximising development outcomes drawing on all available sources of finance, including the promotion of private sector finance and participation.",""],[1,"44","3","Public-Private Partnership Infrastructure Financing","infrastructure projects that are deemed commercially viable and bankable (as well as those that may not be bankable in the immediate-term but could be made bankable in partnership with other stakeholders) shall be pursued through PPP and other innovative financing models.",""],[1,"44","4","Public-Private Partnership Mechanism Strengthening","PPP mechanisms will be further strengthened through the introduction of key legislation, including those relating to procurement, PFM and other relevant areas.",""],[1,"45","2","Priority Infrastructure Project Identification and Financing Mechanism Development","Identify priority infrastructure projects, with a focus on job creation, to be developed together with viable and appropriate financing mechanisms",""],[1,"45","5","Public-Private Partnership Mechanisms for Infrastructure Development","Promote PPP mechanisms which facilitate the development of commercially viable infrastructure projects through greater public- private sector collaboration",""],[1,"45","6","Public-Private Partnership Program for Infrastructure Services","Conditions created for a robust PPP program in Myanmar that gives the government a modality (in addition to traditional public procurement and SEEs) for procuring needed infrastructure services and achieving value for money (PSD-AP Pillar 4)",""],[1,"45","9","Priority Infrastructure Development","Accelerated development of priority infrastructures and introduction of e- government (EP 4)",""],[1,"45","11","Public Procurement Law and Competitive Tendering Reform","Create an enabling environment in which standardized and transparent competitive international tendering for nationally significant projects is the norm, including but not limited to the enactment of a Procurement Law",""],[1,"45","19","Road User Fees Framework Reform","Implement measures to improve road user fees framework, including heavy vehicle license fees, fuel levies, and road tolls",""]],"33":[[1,"45","17","International Transport Corridor Upgrading Programme","Upgrade international transport corridors, such as expanding access to expressways for heavy commercial vehicles, rehabilitating and modernizing the pavement for high traffic highways, and improving road safety",""],[1,"46","1","Domestic Rail Line Expansion, Modernization, and Maintenance","Expand, modernize and maintain domestic rail lines",""],[1,"46","5","National Rural Road Access Program","Improve rural transport connectivity, including through a new National Rural Road Access Program",""],[1,"46","7","Transport Laws, Policies, Programmes, and Strategies Reform","Revise and enhance key transport related laws, polices programmes and strategies",""]],"34":[[1,"20","20","Security Sector Support","Support the security sector to effectively perform its role serving our people and ensuring peace, safety and",""]],"35":[[1,"60","17","Comprehensive Disaster and Climate Risk Management Systems","Establish comprehensive disaster and climate risk management systems",""],[1,"61","3","Shock-Responsive Social Protection and Risk Mitigation Financing","Improve access to shock responsive social protection and risk mitigation financing, taking into consideration gender and the needs of vulnerable groups, to assist preparation for, and recovery from loss and damage resulting from, natural disasters and climate triggered events",""],[1,"61","6","Adaptive Capacity and Resilience Strengthening for Vulnerable Households, Communities, and Sectors","Increase the adaptive capacity of vulnerable households, communities and sectors so that they are resilient to the adverse impacts of natural disasters including climate triggered events",""]],"36":[[1,"61","13","Water Conservation and Water-Related Infrastructure Investment","Myanmar will enhance investments in conservation and in water-related infrastructure.",""],[1,"61","13","Township Water Use Planning and Hygiene Promotion","The GoM will also promote township-level water use planning and encourage healthy water use practices, in order to ensure that the water supply, sanitation and hygiene needs of our schools, health facilities, urban, private sector, and rural communities are met.",""],[1,"62","4","Catchment-Based Integrated Water Resources Planning and Management","Introduce catchment-based integrated water resources planning and management to ensure that water resources are used equitably and sustainably and are responsive to gender-specific needs",""],[1,"62","6","National and Sub-national Water Supply Service Inventory and Upgrade Programme","Develop national and sub- national inventories of existing water supply services, repair and/or upgrade existing water supply services, and prepare plans for the development of new water supply services",""],[1,"62","9","Township and Village Water Safety Plans","Develop township and village water safety plans, including ensuring the provision of clean and safe water to all people",""],[1,"62","12","Cross-Border Water Cooperation Mechanism","Facilitate greater cross- border, regional and international collaboration on water related matters in partnership with sub- national governments",""],[1,"62","14","Safe Water Handling and Use Promotion","Increase people's use of safe practices for the handling and use of water for domestic and drinking purposes",""],[1,"62","20","Household and Community Safe Hygiene Promotion","Enable greater knowledge, attitude and practice of safe hygiene at household and community levels",""]],"37":[[1,"62","17","Environmentally Safe Waste Management and Disposal","Practice effective and environmentally safe waste management and disposal in industrial, commercial, household, and public- sector use contexts",""]],"38":[[1,"63","3","Sustainable Energy Sector Development and Investment Promotion","Myanmar will prioritise the long-term benefits gained by managing the safe and sustainable development of our energy sector, including ensuring careful consideration of available energy resources, together with analysis of consumption patterns and future projections.",""],[1,"63","3","Renewable Energy Investment-Friendly Environment","The country will also prioritise the creation of an investment friendly environment which encourages the use of innovative, sustainable and renewable energy generation technologies.",""],[1,"63","11","Renewable Energy Scale-Up Programme","Scale-up use of renewable energy resources such as wind, solar, hydro, geothermal and bio-energy in partnership and with agreement of local populations",""],[1,"63","14","National and Sub-national Energy Development Planning","Develop and implement comprehensive national and sub-national energy development plans, prioritising least-cost generation expansion,",""],[1,"64","3","Policy and Regulatory Reform for Energy Investment","Facilitate policy, legal, regulatory and broader good governance actions which will enable greater investment and private sector participation in energy generation and provision",""],[1,"64","5","Energy Efficiency and Conservation Promotion","Promote energy generation and distribution efficiency and conservation in industry, commercial, household, and public- sector use",""],[1,"64","8","Cross-Border Energy Collaboration Mechanism","Facilitate greater cross- border, regional and international collaboration in energy matters in partnership with State and Region governments",""],[1,"64","10","Electricity Pricing and Subsidy Policy Reform","Formulate policies to inform appropriate electricity product pricing (including appropriate use of subsidies) which strike an appropriate balance between needs of producers and consumers",""],[1,"64","15","Private Sector Participation and Energy Provider Privatization Reform","Create an enabling environment which promotes greater private sector participation in energy generation and supply including privatization of State- owned energy providers",""]],"39":[[1,"65","1","Sustainable Land and Natural Resource Management Policy","To address these and related challenges, Myanmar will prioritise policies focused on long-term sustainable land management, including protecting and sustainably managing our nation's forests, rivers, mangroves, mountain areas, lakes and coastal areas, and developing the necessary institutions at all levels required to manage our natural resources in a sustainable manner.",""],[1,"65","1","Natural Capital Valuation and Transparent Resource Management Regime","Quantifying the value of our natural resource wealth will be one important step towards a more effective and transparent management regime, which must include continued engagement with affected communities.",""],[1,"65","1","Natural Capital Integration into Planning and Budgeting","Considering natural capital value, and its contribution to the economy and the lives of our people, in sectoral and economic planning, budgeting and policies will be essential to improving natural resource management.",""],[1,"65","4","Land Governance and Sustainable Resource Industry Management","Improve land governance and sustainable management of resource-based industries ensuring our natural resources dividend benefits all our people",""],[1,"65","5","Natural Resource Regulatory Framework and Enforcement Mechanisms","Establish a comprehensive, clear and coherent regulatory framework that informs the sustainable management, exploitation and trade of natural resources supported by appropriate enforcement mechanisms",""],[1,"65","6","Transparent Extractive Revenue Management Mechanism","Use innovative mechanisms to more effectively and transparently manage revenues generated from the extractive industries for the longer-term benefit of the country",""],[1,"65","8","Minerals Sector Reform for Sustainability and Profitability","Reform the nature of the minerals sector such that it becomes both sustainable and profitable, while making both a positive contribution to",""],[1,"66","2","EITI Implementation Acceleration Measures","Greatly accelerate all necessary measures to meet requirements for EITI implementation",""],[1,"66","4","Environmental Safeguards and Regulatory Controls for Natural Resource-Based Industries","Strengthen and enforce environmental safeguards and regulatory controls regarding natural resources-based industries",""]],"40":[[1,"66","11","Urban Governance and Land Management Policy Framework Strengthening","Strengthen urban governance and related policy frameworks, including those related to urban land management, with a focus on gender- specific and youth-related concerns",""],[1,"66","12","Urban Infrastructure and Services Resilience Enhancement","Increase resilience of urban infrastructure and services to protect from climate change, disasters, shocks and other natural hazards",""],[1,"66","15","Urban Infrastructure Resilience Retrofitting","Design and/or assess and retrofit urban infrastructure to improve resilience to natural and man-made disasters and other shock events, with a focus on reducing carbon",""],[1,"67","2","Integration of Quality of Life Measures into Urban Planning","Ensure that quality of life considerations such as water management (retention and reticulation) and expansion of public spaces (centres of learning/libraries, parks, playgrounds and green areas) are fully integrated into urban planning frameworks and decision making",""],[1,"67","6","Municipal Solid Waste Management and Recycling Education","Provide efficient public municipal services including solid waste collection and management systems combined with public education on recycling and waste minimization practices",""],[1,"67","8","National Housing Strategy and Affordable Housing Programme","Develop and effectively implement a national housing strategy, including low-cost housing and housing for vulnerable groups, and implement affordable housing projects including resettlement of squatters and the improvement of slum areas",""],[1,"68","1","Urban Land and Property Rights Strengthening","Strengthen urban households' land rights/tenure and property rights and enforcement",""]],"41":[[1,"67","4","Sustainable Public Transport Development","Develop sustainable public transport systems, including school transportation systems, that are safe, convenient and accessible to all",""],[1,"67","5","Priority Infrastructure Development and E-Government Introduction","Accelerated development of priority infrastructures and introduction of e- government",""]],"42":[[1,"67","9","Tourism Sector Reform Package","Implement a comprehensive package of reforms focused on achieving sustainable expansion of the tourism sector in ways that contribute to economic development and the socio-cultural life of our people",""],[1,"68","3","Creative and Cultural Heritage Industry Development and Protection","Develop and protect creative and cultural heritage industries such as cultural and eco-tourism and related high-value services industries",""]],"43":[[1,"69","2","MSDP High-Level Implementation Coordination Structures","Naturally, coordinating the implementation of the MSDP will require the GoM to establish dedicated high-level structures, appropriately supported at the administrative level.",""],[1,"69","2","Cross-Ministerial and Stakeholder Coordination for MSDP Implementation","The GoM will also need to strengthen cooperation, collaboration and coordination amongst all relevant ministries and government entities, and also with the broadest range of national and international stakeholders - key amongst these being our local civil society organisations and private sector.",""],[1,"69","3","MSDP Implementation Oversight and Coordination Unit","The Ministry of Planning and Finance (MoPF) shall serve as the focal entity responsible for overseeing implementation of the MSDP, and for housing the MSDP Implementation Unit (MSDP-IU).","Ministry of Planning and Finance (MoPF)"],[1,"69","3","MSDP Implementation Unit Strategic Support Function","The MSDP-IU shall be responsible for providing general guidance, approving strategic decisions, and solving strategic issues which may arise during the implementation of the MSDP.",""],[1,"69","5","MSDP Implementation Unit Monitoring and Support Mechanism","The MSDP-IU will actively support the implementation of the MSDP by providing the Planning Commission with monitoring update reports that includes clear analysis and technical proposals to overcome any issues or problems that may arise.",""],[1,"69","6","MSDP Implementation and Coordination Mechanism","The MSDP-IU shall work through existing structures where possible and oversee the creation of new implementation structures, coordination frameworks and monitoring mechanisms where needed.",""]],"44":[[1,"69","7","Comprehensive Financing Strategy for MSDP Implementation","Effective implementation of the MSDP will also require a comprehensive financing strategy.",""],[1,"70","5","MSDP Financing Strategy Development","the MSDP-IU will develop a more complete MSDP financing strategy, assessing strengths and weaknesses, and the risks and opportunities involved when linking various sources of finance to various strategies and Action Plans.",""],[1,"70","6","International Public Finance Mobilization and Channeling Mechanism","the MSDP-IU shall ensure that international public finance is mobilised and channelled into relevant priority sectors and projects in accordance with both the MSDP and guided by the DACU and Development Assistance Policy (DAP).",""],[1,"70","9","Project Bank Creation","the MSDP-IU will oversee the creation of a Project Bank.",""],[1,"70","10","Project Bank for MSDP Development Projects","The Project Bank shall consist of specific development projects linked to various Action Plans which make up this MSDP.",""],[1,"70","11","Public Investment Programme","Major capital projects that meet predetermined criteria will be elevated further into a Public Investment Programme.",""],[1,"70","12","Project Screening and Appraisal Framework","The MSDP-IU will produce a general project screening and appraisal framework, together with transparent guidelines and principles for project screening and approval.",""],[1,"70","12","Project Identification and Funding Linkage Process","Furthermore, the MSDP-IU will establish the process and criteria for identifying the aforementioned projects and facilitate linkages to the most appropriate source of funding.",""],[1,"70","13","PPP Guidance for National Development Projects","The MSDP-IU will also provide guidance on the use of PPP that will encourage the role of the private sector and attract greater private capital in the implementation of national development projects.",""],[1,"70","14","Project Solicitation Support by MSDP-IU","The MSDP-IU will at all times remain supportive of government entities and encourage them to be proactive in soliciting the projects they plan to develop.",""]],"45":[[1,"71","1","Government-wide Monitoring and Evaluation Framework","A coherent and consistent government-wide monitoring and evaluation (M&E) Framework will be critical in the implementation of the MSDP in terms of tracking and measuring its effectiveness, efficiency, sustainability and impact throughout and following the implementation period.",""],[1,"71","2","MSDP Monitoring and Evaluation Framework Development","A M&E Framework will be developed by the MSDP-IU which will focus on a comprehensive results framework including inputs, processes, outputs, outcomes and impacts.",""],[1,"71","3","Action Plan Linkage and M&E Framework Development","Specific programmes and projects will be linked to specific Action Plans that will contribute towards the achievement of each of the strategies and goals expressed within the MSDP.",""],[1,"71","3","Strategy and Project-Level Monitoring and Evaluation Frameworks","Associated and subsidiary M&E Frameworks at the strategy and project/programme level shall be designed and implemented.",""],[1,"71","4","MSDP Monitoring and Evaluation Framework Implementation","In the implementation of the M&E Framework that will encompass all aspects of MSDP implementation, it is important to define specific, measurable, achievable, relevant and time-bound indicators (targets) and means of verification.",""],[1,"71","5","MSDP Baseline Assessment and M&E Indicator Development","The setting of additional indicators that will inform the MSDP M&E Framework shall build upon this report, while accounting for potential heterogeneity in robustness and reliability of indicators.",""],[1,"71","5","Baseline Studies for Projects and Programmes","For projects and programmes where indicators are either missing or of limited reliability, further baseline studies will be",""],[1,"71","7","Annual Project and Programme Progress Reporting","annual reports on the progress and performance of projects and programmes against specified outcomes shall be submitted to the MoPF at pre-specified dates as part of the implementation of this MSDP.","MoPF"],[1,"72","1","Coherent Government M&E Standard Development","the GoM plans to devise a coherent M&E standard to generate consistent and comparable performance data across government.","CSO | PAPRD | MDI | relevant line ministries"],[1,"72","7","Biennial MSDP Progress Review Process","Progress toward MSDP completion will undergo a thorough review every two years from the date of issuance.",""],[1,"73","4","MSDP Review, Revision, and Updating Process","The GoM will continue to review, revise and update this MSDP as progress is made, as context and events evolve, and as new plans and strategies are developed.",""]],"46":[[1,"72","2","Stakeholder Engagement Strategy for MSDP Implementation","An engagement strategy that involves active and regular consultations with multiple stakeholders will be deployed to ensure transparency and accountability in the implementation of this MSDP and the associated M&E standard.",""],[1,"72","3","MSDP Online Implementation Information Portal","An online portal with information regarding the implementation of this MSDP shall be established to inform the public on inputs, outputs, outcomes, efficiency and processes of implementation.",""],[1,"72","4","Online Platform Public Awareness Campaigns","The online platform shall be coupled with public awareness campaigns targeted to",""],[1,"72","6","Public Consultation Events for MSDP Implementation","The government shall also hold public consultation events to receive feedback and comments regarding MSDP implementation.",""]]}});